</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Convergence of Gradient-Based Sampling</h3>

<div id="A3.Thmstatement3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_statement">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmstatement3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statement 3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmstatement3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convergence of Gradient-Based Sampling)<span id="A3.Thmstatement3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be an Equilibrium Matching model with corresponding energy function <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla E(x)=f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla E(x)=f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth and bounded below by <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(x)\geq E_{\text{inf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">inf</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(x)\geq E_{\text{inf}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, gradient descent with step size <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in\bigl[0,\tfrac{1}{L}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in\bigl[0,\tfrac{1}{L}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{0\leq k&lt;K}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\leq\frac{2\bigl(E(x_{0})-E_{\text{inf}}\bigr)}{\eta\,K}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">inf</mtext></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{0\leq k&lt;K}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\leq\frac{2\bigl(E(x_{0})-E_{\text{inf}}\bigr)}{\eta\,K},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the iterate after <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> steps and <math id="A3.Thmstatement3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of optimization steps performed.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Derivation of Statement <a href="#S4.Thmstatement3" title="Statement 3 (Convergence of Gradient-Based Sampling). ‣ 4 Analysis ‣ Equilibrium Matching: Generative Modeling with Implicit Energy-Based Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E(y)\,\leq\,E(x)+\nabla E(x)^{\top}(y-x)+\frac{L}{2}\,\|y-x\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">≤</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(y)\,\leq\,E(x)+\nabla E(x)^{\top}(y-x)+\frac{L}{2}\,\|y-x\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\,f(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\,f(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and recall <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla E(x_{k})=-f(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla E(x_{k})=-f(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E(x_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E(x_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq E(x_{k})-\eta\,f(x_{k})^{\top}f(x_{k})+\tfrac{L}{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq E(x_{k})-\eta\,f(x_{k})^{\top}f(x_{k})+\tfrac{L}{2}\,\eta^{2}\,\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=E(x_{k})-\eta\Bigl(1-\tfrac{L\eta}{2}\Bigr)\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\;\;\geq\;\;E(x_{k})-\tfrac{\eta}{2}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.838em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=E(x_{k})-\eta\Bigl(1-\tfrac{L\eta}{2}\Bigr)\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\;\;\geq\;\;E(x_{k})-\tfrac{\eta}{2}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality holds because <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq 1/L\implies 1-\tfrac{L\eta}{2}\geq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq 1/L\implies 1-\tfrac{L\eta}{2}\geq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing from <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=K-1</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E(x_{K})-E(x_{0})\;\leq\;-\tfrac{\eta}{2}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\;\leq\;-\tfrac{\eta}{2}\,K\,\min_{0\leq k&lt;K}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">≤</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.058em">≤</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>K</mi><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(x_{K})-E(x_{0})\;\leq\;-\tfrac{\eta}{2}\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\;\leq\;-\tfrac{\eta}{2}\,K\,\min_{0\leq k&lt;K}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(x_{K})\geq E_{\mathrm{inf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>inf</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(x_{K})\geq E_{\mathrm{inf}}</annotation></semantics></math>, rearrange to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{0\leq k&lt;K}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{2\bigl(E(x_{0})-E_{\mathrm{inf}}\bigr)}{\eta\,K}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>inf</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{0\leq k&lt;K}\|f(x_{k})\|^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{2\bigl(E(x_{0})-E_{\mathrm{inf}}\bigr)}{\eta\,K},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">as required.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Relation between Integration-Based and Optimization-Based Sampling</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>ODE Sampling as a Special Case of Optimization</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the ODE</p>
<table id="A4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}=v(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}=v(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and its explicit (forward) Euler discretization with a uniform time grid on <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}+h\,v(x_{k}),\qquad h=\tfrac{1}{N},\;k=0,\dots,N-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}+h\,v(x_{k}),\qquad h=\tfrac{1}{N},\;k=0,\dots,N-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">When the velocity field is conservative with potential <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)=-\nabla E(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)=-\nabla E(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, the Euler step becomes:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-h\,\nabla E(x_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-h\,\nabla E(x_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which is exactly a gradient-descent update with step size <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=h=\tfrac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=h=\tfrac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, with <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps on a unit time horizon, the gradient-descent sampler with <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\tfrac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\tfrac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with the explicit Euler ODE sampler.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>General Integration Samplers</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The equivalence above suggests a broader correspondence: integration-based samplers can be interpreted as optimization-based methods by viewing the velocity as a descent direction. In particular, when <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)=-\nabla E(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)=-\nabla E(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, any time integrator induces an optimization update rule.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Practically, ODE samplers in generative modeling are often implemented on a uniform grid with step size <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\tfrac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\tfrac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the optimization view, we are not bound to this constraint. We can adopt adaptive step sizes while retaining the same underlying direction field. This perspective enables a direct adaptation of existing integration-based samplers within Equilibrium Matching.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
